{"id": "EUVD-2026-101211", "enisaUuid": "edeb32c3-760c-3f28-8ab2-373a3450b673", "description": "OW2 ASM 5.0 before 9.11 contains an excessive memory allocation vulnerability in ClassReader.readBootstrapMethodsAttribute() that sizes an int array from num_bootstrap_methods without validating attribute_length. Attackers can supply a crafted class file of about 100 bytes that forces roughly 2 GB allocation, causing an OutOfMemoryError that crashes the JVM or consuming thread.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T14:16:30", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T15:55:22", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://gitlab.ow2.org/asm/asm/-/merge_requests/456", "https://gitlab.ow2.org/asm/asm/-/commit/eb5fa95bb0670eaec2ecf9b8a3a501b48e5a967c", "https://gitlab.ow2.org/asm/asm/-/blob/ASM_9_10_1/asm/src/main/java/org/objectweb/asm/ClassReader.java#L3497", "https://asm.ow2.io/versions.html", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ow2-asm-5.0-before-9.11-excessive-memory-allocation-via-bootstrapmethods-attribute"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110257", "GHSA-jv96-63p8-4rfx"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "38cd480d-b0c5-3f0c-ade4-1eeab4e7a43d", "product": {"name": "ASM", "vendor": {"name": "OW2"}}, "product_version": "5.0 <9.11"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6b3ff30a-a4c4-3123-827e-bd0c12b24e6e", "vendor": {"name": "OW2"}}], "isExploited": false}